"""Measured tail rotor power of the UH-60A in level flight: the Airloads Program flights 84-90 (sixth-year production
aircraft with the ESSS fairings, wire strike kit and test instrumentation), from the intermediate shaft torque, as
plotted in the JAHS 2004 performance paper (fig. 4) against the main rotor's advance ratio at six weight
coefficients C_W = W / (rho A (Omega R)^2) of the main rotor. Digitized at 300 dpi (symbols located by pixel; two
merged pairs split; ~0.002 in mu, ~0.00004 in C_P).

C_P_TR is taken as the tail rotor's own power coefficient P / (rho A_TR (Omega R)_TR^3): at mu 0.2-0.25 it gives
40-70 hp, in line with the tail rotor power of the 77-17 level flights. The paper does not list the weights and
altitudes; the model is flown at 16,500 lb and the density that gives each C_W."""

